+The pipeline combines calibrated Isolation Forest waveform scores, an LSTM reconstruction detector, a GRU synthetic-life regressor, and a healthy-reference deviation check. Deep models need 24 consecutive samples at the training interval (default 5 seconds). A waveform alarm can be reported during warmup, but trend health and RUL remain unavailable.
 
-## Quickstart
+`is_anomaly` can be `null`: unknown is different from normal. The health index is a heuristic display index, not a failure probability. RUL is displayed as a normalized synthetic estimate. The API's simulated hours use the recorded simulator horizon, never a hardcoded 240 hours; non-simulation sources receive no hours. Residual-based intervals are evaluated on held-out synthetic data and provide no real-world coverage guarantee.
 
